  "scenario": "A high-volume 300 mm logic fab making a mature logic device has seen functional die yield drop about 20% over the past six weeks, holding low across many lots. The dip began after a scheduled preventive-maintenance window on the etch and deposition tools. Process engineers' leading theories are a pressure or temperature setpoint drift, so they favor retuning those setpoints. Inline inspection has flagged more defects than usual on a mid-line layer. Standard tool logs read broadly within spec. The etch, deposition, clean, and filtration modules are all adjustable. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available process controls, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the loss and what to do about it.",
